  "physics": {
    "_comment": "Arcade driving feel, shared by all vehicles. grip / steerFast are picked between their two numbers using each type's 'handling' (first number = handling 0, second = handling 1). steerSlow/steerFast = how far the front wheels turn (radians) when crawling / at top speed. handbrakeGrip = how little the tyres hold while the handbrake is on (lower = longer drifts). slideGrip is used once the car is already sliding sideways faster than slideSpeed. stepMax = highest kerb a vehicle climbs; anything taller is a wall. launchMinRise = how fast (m/s) a ramp must be lifting the car for it to jump at the top. lateralAccel = how hard a vehicle can corner (m/s², by handling).",
